graph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA8</code><description>Consider PNC warning - 'Drugs'</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>Where this offence was committed near school premises, by using a courier under the age of 18 or within a custodial institution, section 72 of the Sentencing Act 2020 provides that this has to be treated as an aggravating factor in sentencing.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><description>EITHER WAY</description></modeoftrial><t